// Generated by transModule
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : data/scripts/SpawnDefs/InfoNPCs/_src/ToughZone_Info_NPC.xls 	Sheet : DarkAstoria_Info 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 38 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable RestrictedText :
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P3151863595" "This Hazard zone is what is known as 'Dark Astoria.'  Though you cannot see far due to the dense fog in the area, you are in a sort of modern age ghost town.  The citizens have perished, but this place is by no means vacant.  For the unwary Hero, it's also a death sentence.  If you hope to maintain that heartbeat in your chest, you should find some friends or colleagues to help you.  Otherwise, one of the spectral wanderers may, sooner rather than later, be you.<br><br>See my report for more information.  It should give you an idea what to expect:<br><br><face heading><span align=center><font color=PaleGoldenRod>RECONNAISSANCE REPORT</font></face></span><scale 1.5><span align=center><color red>*** Approved Use Only ***</color></scale></span><br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>History:</scale></color><br>Formerly known as Astoria, this is a place where crumbling magics hold a horrible dark god from the ancient world barely in check.  As Mot's bonds loosen, his influence spreads, raising the dead and causing havoc and horror.<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Hostiles Strength:</scale></color><br>Levels 21 through 29<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Suggested Squad Parameters:</scale></color><br>3-person to 5-person teams<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Highlights:</scale></color><br><br><color orange><b>- Dense Fog</color></b><br>The entire landscape is covered in such a heavy fog that it appears nearly twilight even during the day.<br><br><color orange><b>- Ghostly Citizens</color></b><br>Several citizens perished and their ghosts remain, walking the streets of Dark Astoria.  Get too close and they disappear.<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Identified Hostiles:</color></scale><br>- Banished Pantheon<br>- Circle of Thorns<br>- Tsoo<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Amenities:</color></scale><br>- St. Elegius Hospital<br><br>"
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
"P2366009989" "<em=lecture>If you're new to Dark Astoria, {HeroName}, I'll give you a quick debriefing of the area if you're interested.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Leave :
// DisplayName for N_DarkAstoria_Info :

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated by transModule
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : data/scripts/SpawnDefs/InfoNPCs/_src/ToughZone_Info_NPC.xls 	Sheet : DarkAstoriaRevamp_Info 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 38 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable RestrictedText :
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P120152873" "I don’t know what malignant force brought you here but you are now in the place known as 'Dark Astoria.'  Not far from here, the dark god Mot stirs from his slumber, intent on devouring us all.  Do not give up hope though! Both heroes and villains who have reached the pinnacles of their training and have begun to unlock their Incarnate powers have been known to survive for a time on these forsaken streets.<br><br>If you have found yourself here, uncertain on how to proceed, look for either <color gold>Captain Nolan</color> or <color gold>‘The Arachnos Threat’</color> among your contacts.<br><br>See my report for more information.  It should give you an idea what to expect:<br><br><face heading><span align=center><font color=PaleGoldenRod>RECONNAISSANCE REPORT</font></face></span><scale 1.5><span align=center><color red>*** Approved Use Only ***</color></scale></span><br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>History:</scale></color><br>The fog that has gripped Dark Astoria for years has receded, revealing a place filled with evil.  Mot’s influence is nearly complete, but it is not just his followers that roam these streets threatening the unfortunate souls that have found themselves trapped here.<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Hostiles Strength:</scale></color><br>Levels 50 through 54<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Suggested Squad Parameters:</scale></color><br>1-person to 3-person teams. 1-person to 5-person teams in Moth Cemetery<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Neighborhoods:</scale></color><br><br><color orange><b>- Romero Heights</color></b><br>The Bulwark can be found here, offering protection.  <color Red>Level Range: 50</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Barca Plaza</color></b><br>Beware of the Tsoo that guard this neighborhood.  <color Gold>Scintillating Prism</color> can be found here, offering protection. <color Red>Level Range: 50 to 51</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Toffet Terrace</color></b><br>Watch out for the Knives of Vengeance that prowl these streets.  The protected area known as <color gold>The Rose Lamp</color> can be found here. <color Red>Level Range: 51 to 52</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Raimi Arcade</color></b><br>The Circle of Thorns control this neighborhood.  While here, seek out <color gold>Fading Nimbus</color> or <color gold>Flicker</color> for sanctuary. <color Red>Level Range: 52 to 53</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Dido’s View</color></b><br>Talons of Vengeance threaten all who enter here. <color gold>Illuminous</color> offers protection in this neighborhood. <color Red>Level Range: 53 to 54</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Moth Cemetery</color></b><br>Banished Pantheon maintain unwavering control over the Cemetery. It is here that Mot’s sway is absolute. There is no protection to be found amongst the desecrated monuments so be cautious. Enemies here are more numerous than anywhere else. <color Red>Level Range: 54</color><br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Identified Hostiles:</color></scale><br>- Banished Pantheon<br>- Circle of Thorns<br>- Tsoo<br>- Talons of Vengeance<br>- Knives of Vengeance<br>- Knives of Artemis<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Amenities:</color></scale><br>- St. Elegius Hospital<br><br>"
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
"P3869261720" "<em=lecture>If you're newly arrived here in Dark Astoria, {HeroName}, I'll tell you what you need to know to survive.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Leave :
// DisplayName for N_DarkAstoria_Info :

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated by transModule
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : data/scripts/SpawnDefs/InfoNPCs/_src/ToughZone_Info_NPC.xls 	Sheet : DarkAstoriaRevampGV_Info 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 38 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable RestrictedText :
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P795725398" "Before you is the portal to Dark Astoria, a forsaken place where the dark god Mot threatens our very existence.  It is not adviseable to enter this portal unless you have reached the pinnacle of your powers as a villain and have begun on your path as an Incarnate.<br><br>If you feel you are ready but are uncertain on how to proceed, look for <Color Gold>'An Arachnos Threat'</color> among your contacts.<br><br>See my report for more information.  It should give you an idea what to expect:<br><br><face heading><span align=center><font color=PaleGoldenRod>RECONNAISSANCE REPORT</font></face></span><scale 1.5><span align=center><color red>*** Approved Use Only ***</color></scale></span><br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>History:</scale></color><br>The fog that has gripped Dark Astoria for years has receded, revealing a place filled with evil.  Mot’s influence is nearly complete, but it is not just his followers that roam these streets threatening the unfortunate souls that have found themselves trapped here.<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Hostiles Strength:</scale></color><br>Levels 50 through 54<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Suggested Squad Parameters:</scale></color><br>1-person to 3-person teams. 1-person to 5-person teams in Moth Cemetery<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Neighborhoods:</scale></color><br><br><color orange><b>- Romero Heights</color></b><br>The Bulwark can be found here, offering protection.  <color Red>Level Range: 50</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Barca Plaza</color></b><br>Beware of the Tsoo that guard this neighborhood.  <color Gold>Scintillating Prism</color> can be found here, offering protection. <color Red>Level Range: 50 to 51</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Toffet Terrace</color></b><br>Watch out for the Knives of Vengeance that prowl these streets.  The protected area known as <color gold>The Rose Lamp</color> can be found here. <color Red>Level Range: 51 to 52</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Raimi Arcade</color></b><br>The Circle of Thorns control this neighborhood.  While here, seek out <color gold>Fading Nimbus</color> or <color gold>Flicker</color> for sanctuary. <color Red>Level Range: 52 to 53</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Dido’s View</color></b><br>Talons of Vengeance threaten all who enter here. <color gold>Illuminous</color> offers protection in this neighborhood. <color Red>Level Range: 53 to 54</color><br><br><color orange><b>- Moth Cemetery</color></b><br>Banished Pantheon maintain unwavering control over the Cemetery. It is here that Mot’s sway is absolute. There is no protection to be found amongst the desecrated monuments so be cautious. Enemies here are more numerous than anywhere else. <color Red>Level Range: 54</color><br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Identified Hostiles:</color></scale><br>- Banished Pantheon<br>- Circle of Thorns<br>- Tsoo<br>- Talons of Vengeance<br>- Knives of Vengeance<br>- Knives of Artemis<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Amenities:</color></scale><br>- St. Elegius Hospital<br><br>"
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
"P2072301356" "<em=lecture>Before you cross this threshold into Dark Astoria, {HeroName}, there are things you need to know in order to survive.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Leave :
// DisplayName for N_DarkAstoria_Info :
"P4081916975" "Dark Astoria Reconnaissance Officer"

