// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : data/scripts/SpawnDefs/InfoNPCs/_src/ToughZone_Info_NPC.xls 	Sheet : FortHadesEvent_Info 
//
// Script      : Xlstospawndef.bat 
// Version     : 38 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Script Variable RestrictedText :
// Script Variable InfoText :
"P2373640289" "This is Fort Hades.  If you haven't noticed it yet, it's tougher than the rest of Port Oakes so you will probably need reinforcements in this area.  Oh, and there's something about this Fort you need to understand.  It's no walk in the park here, there are real ghosts haunting this Fort so you best be on your guard at all times.  <br><br>Now, see my report for more information.  It should give you an idea what to expect:<br><br><face heading><span align=center><font color=PaleGoldenRod>RECONNAISSANCE REPORT</font></face></span><span align=center><scale 1.5><color red>*** CONFIDENTIAL ***</color></scale></span><br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>History:</scale></color><br>The pirate Blackbeard had just captured Queen Ann's Revenge and sought a place to test her in battle.  He came upon a newly erected French Fort and used his massive firepower on the half-manned structure.  Upon storming the beach, the French were outarmed and outmanned by Blackbeard's cuthtroats and were soon surrounded.  They asked for quarter but his crew had already tasted blood and cut down brutally to the last one.  The hauntings began soon after.<br><br>These ghosts are of particular interest to Lord Recluse.  He's been studying them, with the help of Ghost Widow, to see if they might be used as an ethereal army.  The problem is that the ghosts are bound to the island and the site of their horrible deaths.<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Hostiles Strength:</scale></color><br>Levels 10 through 12<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Suggested Squad Parameters:</scale></color><br>3 to 5-man teams<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Highlights:</scale></color><br><b><color orange>Spirit Trapping</color></b><br>Spectral Pirates materialize constantly, arising from the ground or simply appearing.  Every ghost who is defeated within 10 feet of a trap has a chance of having it's essence sucked in and held.  As Villains successfully trap ghosts, they are awarded either the Ghost Hunter or Ghost Buster badges.<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Identified Hostiles:</color></scale><br>- Arachnos<br>- Circle of Thorns<br>- Spectral Pirates<br><br><color YellowGreen><scale 1.1>Amenities:</color></scale><br>- Hospital in Arena District<br>- Trainer (Arbiter Unger in Dockside)<br>- Notoriety Contact in Arena District<br><br>"
// Script Variable OutLoudInfoText :
"P2536224317" "<em=lecture>If you're new to Fort Hades, {HeroName}, I'll give you a quick debriefing of the area if you're interested.<em=none>"
// Script Variable Leave :
// DisplayName for N_FortHades_Info :

// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************
// ************************************************************************

